       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen at 15 g/day is a toxic dose, and a single 5 g dose is already in the range where hepatotoxicity is a concern. Nothing you've told me about this patient (70 kg, normal liver and kidney function) makes it safe. I can't see a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate, and it could cause serious or fatal liver injury.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum)\n- 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n\nIf the goal is stronger analgesia than acetaminophen can give, I can enter a different or additional agent if you tell me which one. If this is for a suspected overdose or some other special situation, that needs a toxicology or pharmacy consult, not a standing order. Please let me know how you'd like to proceed."
